+.. _hookimpl_arg_default:
+
+Hookimpl argument defaults
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+A *hookimpl* may also declare a default value for an argument. The value it
+receives is chosen in this order:
+
+1. the value passed by the hook call;
+2. the hookspec's default value for the argument;
+3. the hookimpl's own default value.
+
+The hookimpl default is therefore only used when neither the caller nor the
+hookspec provides the argument, for example when a new *hookimpl* runs
+against an older hookspec that does not have the argument yet:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    @hookimpl
+    def myhook(config, args, new_arg="fallback"):
+        print(new_arg)
+
+This applies to plain hookimpls as well as to :ref:`wrappers <hookwrappers>`
+and :ref:`old-style hookwrappers <old_style_hookwrappers>`.
+
+.. versionchanged:: 1.7
+    Values passed by the hook call or the hookspec's defaults now take
+    precedence over hookimpl argument defaults. Previously the hookimpl's
+    default was always used.
 
 
